@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #0b7a75
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBorderColor #6b7280
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #fdfdfd
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9ca3af

title Tool-to-tool call (request type)\nOne tool calls another along the declared may_call map — a direct in-process call, or relayed across the wire; no session, no ledger, no merge.

participant "Tool A\n(caller)" as A
participant "UniversalNavigatorProxy\n(satellite)" as P
participant "UniversalNavigator\n(SharedServices, main)" as UN
participant "Tool B\n(callee)" as B

A -> P : ask for Tool B along may_call\n(identical tool code either way)
note over P
  TRIAGE by the route's declared proof = none (internal):
  classify this call as tool_to_tool.
  Internal traffic — no session, no render ledger, no merge.
  Read the may_call map: A -> B is declared and non-circular.
  Recursion guard: may_call depth is within bound.
end note

alt Co-resident — Tool B in the same process
  P -> B : direct function call
  alt B answers
    B --> P : result document
    P --> A : result
  else B raises ChatHealthyException
    B --> P : raise (a middle tool never swallows)
    note over P
      The proxy is a navigator: a throw ends here.
      Classify and log with timings at a
      severity matching impact.
    end note
    P --> A : ChatHealthyException surfaces to the caller
  end

else Satellite — Tool B across the wire
  P -> UN : relay across the wire (internal)
  note over UN
    The main accepts the internal wire traffic.
    Re-affirm triage: proof = none, tool_to_tool;
    confirm the may_call map and recursion guard.
  end note
  UN -> B : dispatch (B co-resident with the main)
  alt B answers
    B --> UN : result document
    UN --> P : relay back (internal callback)
    P --> A : result
  else B raises ChatHealthyException
    B --> UN : raise (a middle tool never swallows)
    note over UN
      Every throw ends in a navigator:
      catch, classify, log with timings
      at a severity matching impact.
    end note
    UN --> P : re-raise across the wire
    P --> A : ChatHealthyException surfaces\nto the caller's navigator
  end
end
@enduml
